#### Section 6: Key Handler — The Core Logic (Lines 174–270)

This is the most important function. It runs on every keypress.

**Strict mode behavior:** The user can ONLY advance by pressing the correct key. Wrong keys are rejected (the character doesn't appear).

```
Key pressed → What happens:
```

| Key | Behavior |
|-----|----------|
| **Backspace** | Removes the last typed character. Clears error state. |
| **Tab** | Inserts up to 4 spaces (only if the target expects spaces at that position) |
| **Enter** | Inserts a newline `\n` PLUS all the leading whitespace on the next line automatically |
| **Correct character** | Appends to `userInput`, clears error state |
| **Wrong character** | Increments `wrongAttempts`, highlights current char red, triggers shake animation. Does NOT advance the cursor. |
| **Ctrl/Alt/Meta** | Ignored (prevents shortcuts from interfering) |
| **Non-character keys** (Shift, Caps, etc.) | Ignored |

**Smart Enter behavior (Lines 220–241):**
When the user presses Enter and the next character is `\n`, the app auto-inserts the newline AND all the leading spaces/tabs on the next line. This saves the user from manually typing indentation.

**Timer start:**
The timer starts on the very first keypress (not when the page loads).

