#### Section 7: Computed Stats (Lines 272–296)

```js
const correctChars = userInput.length;          // In strict mode, all typed chars are correct
const totalKeystrokes = userInput.length + wrongAttempts;
const accuracy = Math.round((correctChars / totalKeystrokes) * 100);

const wordsTyped = correctChars / 5;            // Standard: 1 word = 5 characters
const minutes = (endTime - startTime) / 60000;  // Convert ms to minutes
const wpm = Math.round(wordsTyped / minutes);   // Words per minute

const progress = (userInput.length / targetText.length) * 100;  // Progress bar %
```

> [!NOTE]
> **WPM calculation**: Uses the standard formula where 1 "word" = 5 characters, regardless of actual word boundaries. This is how all typing tests work (MonkeyType, TypeRacer, etc.).

